  "prompt_text": "The figure illustrates a hierarchical, time-ordered buildup of many-body terms, showing how increasingly complex clusters are generated from simpler ones. At the bottom left, a “1-Body” level is represented by single-particle units. These combine to form a “2-Body” source, which includes combinations of one- and two-particle groupings and is associated with a highlighted contribution labeled Hi[Δ⟨2⟩]. An upward arrow indicates that this two-body content then feeds into the next level.\n\nThe same pattern continues for “3-Body,” where the generating source now contains a richer set of combinations built from smaller clusters, plus a highlighted three-particle term labeled Hi[Δ⟨3⟩]. This in turn contributes upward to a larger three-particle cluster and to a further highlighted term, Hi[Δ⟨4⟩], suggesting the next stage in the hierarchy.\n\nOverall, the diagram emphasizes a sequential generation mechanism: one-body correlations produce two-body structure, two-body structure helps generate three-body structure, and so on. The large diagonal arrow labeled “Sequential build-up in time” reinforces that higher-order many-body correlations emerge progressively rather than appearing all at once.",
